  "valuation_insights": "Apple Inc. reported a fiscal 2026 total revenue of $478.83 billion, growing approximately 15.1% year over year [C:revenue_growth]. This strong top-line growth was accompanied by an operating income of $158.06 billion, yielding an operating margin of 33.0% [C:operating_margin], which is lower than Microsoft’s 46.8% margin but higher than Alphabet's 32.0% and Oracle's 30.6%, indicating Apple's competitive operating efficiency. Net income attributable to the company reached $132.18 billion with a notable return on average equity of 142.3% [C:return_on_average_equity], reflecting highly effective use of shareholder equity capital. Apple’s diluted EPS was $8.98, delivering a price-to-earnings ratio of about 38.4 based on the closing price of $344.63 [C:pe], suggesting market premium valuation relative to earnings. The company’s total debt (including current portion) to equity ratio stands at 0.70 [C:debt_to_equity], reflecting moderate leverage. Free cash flow was robust at $136.06 billion [C:free_cash_flow], supporting continued shareholder returns and investment. Quarterly revenue for Q4 2026 was $114.48 billion, up 12% year over year, and the diluted EPS was $2.10 [C:quarter_revenue, C:quarter_eps]. \n\nInsight: Apple capped a record fiscal year with a sequential record in operating income margin growth along with a double-digit EPS increase, underscoring operational leverage and premium pricing power beyond simply revenue growth [L000050, L000057].",
